Urgency Justification: Telephone triage reported an insidious history of weight loss culminating tonight in acute, agonizing pain in the upper left abdomen with radiation to the shoulder, accompanied by severe spontaneous epistaxis. Urgent after-hours assessment was mandated to rule out a catastrophic acute splenic event or leukostasis, preventing potential haemodynamic collapse prior to morning clinic hours.

SUBJECTIVE

Chief Complaint: "My left side has felt heavy for weeks, but tonight it suddenly felt like a knife was twisting under my ribs, and my nose won't stop bleeding."
