Functional Status: Currently bent over in a chair, unable to stand upright due to abdominal pain.
Social/Safety Concerns: Living alone; high risk of collapse if internal haemorrhage is occurring.

OBJECTIVE

Vitals: BP: 140/85 | HR: 115 | Temp: 37.8 | RR: 20 | SpO2: 98% | Wt: 70 Kg (down 6 kg)
General: Pale, diaphoretic adult in acute distress, guarding the left abdomen.
