Abdomen: Massive, distinctly firm, and exquisitely tender splenomegaly palpated extending 8 cm below the left costal margin, crossing the midline. Rebound tenderness is absent, but focal extreme tenderness over the splenic pole suggests localized capsular stretching or acute infarction.
